{"title":"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 27","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The face diagonal of a cube has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Find the value of n given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/9/e5905ced3c7d26f28e89dbd734490c2e6eaa4d59.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\sqrt2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcb356b003cccf00cfe1f186d198e5b3181316f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{volume}$\" width=\"50\" height=\"12\" /> of the cube.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2bec0076aa5c1e65a414f42b2e9c44fedb6c2115.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  draw((0,0)--(10,0)--(10,10)--(0,10)--(0,0)); draw((10,0)--(0,10)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(5,5),NE); label(&quot;$s$&quot;,(5,0),S); label(&quot;$s$&quot;,(0,5),W);  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p>If the length of the face diagonal of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, then by using 45-45-90 triangles, the side length of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b85816a4bd2e620f9db5513337063f3b639dd780.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />.  Thus, the volume of the cube is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/6/ee618f3704c5de61d7df2087ac4b8fc9f70d8180.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 \\sqrt{2})^3 = 16 \\sqrt{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"122\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/9/4c9f7ec7becf2235bc4927bfc8094069aa784a4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{16}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_27&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest\" title=\"2007 iTest\">2007 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Answer_Key\" title=\"2007 iTest Answer Key\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_26\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 26\">Problem 26</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_iTest_Problems/Problem_28\" title=\"2007 iTest Problems/Problem 28\">Problem 28</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<